\author{Compiled by Claude Sonnet 5.5 (claude-sonnet-5-5) for Andr\'as Kornai}
\date{}
\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section{Introduction}
Central Bikol (ISO 639-3 bcl; Glottocode cent2087) is an Austronesian language of the Bicol region of Luzon, Philippines. Its standard written form is based on the Canaman dialect and is used in literature, Catholic rites and mass media. Under the Philippine K-12 programme (Republic Act 10533), Mother Tongue-Based Multilingual Education requires the mother tongue as medium of instruction from Kindergarten to Grade 3. Search results suggested that Bikol Naga was chosen as the regional L1 although the provinces differ in dialect.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No DepEd Central Bikol textbooks or primers were returned directly by search. The research below discusses mother tongue education in the region and should be used to locate official materials through DepEd and Bicol University.
\begin{itemize}
\item Bicol University journal article (Lorenzana). \url{https://systems.bicol-u.edu.ph/journal/assets/journal_pdf/4%20Lorenzana_49-61.pdf}
\item Social Science Diliman journal article. \url{https://journals.upd.edu.ph/index.php/socialsciencediliman/article/download/4402/3995}
\end{itemize}

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item McKaughan and Macaraya, Bikol Dictionary (University of Hawaii), a bilingual Bikol-English and English-Bikol dictionary with an introduction to alphabet and phonology. \url{https://scholarspace.manoa.hawaii.edu/items/422e4ede-08f7-400e-b0f2-28cfe5abaf61/full}
\item Related University of Hawaii ScholarSpace item, found in search results (Mintz Bikol materials, including grammar notes were described in the results). \url{https://scholarspace.manoa.hawaii.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/45aff48a-d303-4ab8-b619-327e3f0f0b2d/content}
\item Margate, glossary of Central Bikol rice-farming lexis aimed at MTB-MLE. \url{https://www.journalofnaturestudies.org/files/JNS21-2/15-31_Margate_Documenting%20Reclaiming%20Lexis.pdf}
\item Wikipedia, Central Bikol. \url{https://www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bikolano}
\item Project MUSE book record. \url{https://muse.jhu.edu/book/61273}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
Search noted that Central Bikol is used in Catholic religious rites. No specific scripture or community URLs were returned.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
No audio or software resources were found in these searches.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Central Bikol is a language of instruction under MTB-MLE for the early grades. Gaps found: no current classroom-oriented grammar or dictionary was surfaced, and materials beyond Grade 3 appear scarce. Dialect variation across the six provinces is a design issue.

\end{document}
